pr_body:
This patch implements `expect.poll()` method that polls given
predicate until a given synchronous matcher succeeds.

Usage:

```js
// wait until page gets 3 frames.
await expect.poll(() => page.frames().length, {
  timeout: 1000,
  message: 'custom error message',
}).toBe(3);
```

Fixes #10235

comments:
I think it necessary to clarify how exactly this feature request will work.

I copied this line from a [comment](https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/issues/10187#issuecomment-964600993) in the initial issue as the proposed usage:

```ts
expect(page.locator('[e2e-target="summary-cost"]').getAttribute('e2e-data').then((value: string): number => Number(value))).greaterThan(1000);
```

Technically to achieve this we may need to rewrite the promise prototype methods, at least to design and change the interface used by internal methods like `locator.getAttribute`, to get the function(s) that is passed so that we can re-run.
Semantically it looks like redesigning promises, as we know a standard promise's resolved value never changes.

So this feature request, if accepted, seems more likely to be implemented in a way similar to the wait-for methods (e.g., [`page.waitForFunction`](https://playwright.dev/docs/api/class-page/#page-wait-for-function)),

```ts
const asyncPredicate = () => (
  page.locator('[e2e-target="summary-cost"]').getAttribute('e2e-data').then((value: string): number => Number(value))
);
await expect(asyncPredicate).toBeGreaterThan(5, { timeout: 3000 });
```

or

```ts
const asyncPredicate = async () => (
  Number(await page.locator('[e2e-target="summary-cost"]').getAttribute('e2e-data'))
);
await expect(asyncPredicate).toBeGreaterThan(5, { timeout: 3000 });
```

that wrap with functions, right?
